# Preserve the delivery order: faithful port first, compatibility and quality-of-life…

Preserve the delivery order: faithful port first, compatibility and
quality-of-life improvements second, richer community mod content third.

## Acceptance criteria

- [ ] Preserve the delivery order: faithful port first, compatibility and
  quality-of-life improvements second, richer community mod content third.

## Code-first faithful-port order — 2026-09-13

The faithful port is code-first, not asset-first. Runtime behavior must be
understood from the preserved reference and source evidence and implemented in
Unreal before final asset conversion becomes a delivery blocker.

The required order is:

1. establish the Unreal runtime foundation and gameplay contracts;
1. build the complete source-faithful world, including levels, interiors,
   props, placement, collision, and streaming;
1. make one default player character and one default vehicle controllable in
   that world with representative cameras and interaction;
1. complete gameplay systems, rendering/shader behavior, saves, loading, audio,
   traffic, pedestrians, damage, recovery, and other runtime code;
1. port missions, objectives, menus, roster, progression, and structured
   content on top of that completed runtime;
1. only then finalize character and vehicle assets, animations, presentation,
   and asset-by-asset equivalence;
1. finish packaging, mods, release hardening, and final parity verification.

Placeholder or representative assets are acceptable during the early runtime
phases when they preserve the behavioral contract. They must never become
source authority or excuse invented transforms, gameplay values, or final
presentation.

